    {
      "id": "3cf7ffb8-9449-48c5-9a13-237f727561a4",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Findings\n\nAcross **33 complete seasons** (1993/94 → 2025/26) and 11,983 matches\n(289 duplicate fixtures dropped), the Ligue 1 record book:\n\n- **Most championships**: Paris Saint-Germain **13** — including ten of\n  the last eleven titles. Lyon 7, Monaco 3, Bordeaux 2, Lille 2, Nantes 2,\n  and one each for Auxerre and Lens.\n- **Champion hall of fame**: PSG's 2015/16 side owns almost every record\n  — **102 points** (a Ligue 1 record, from a 40-game season), fewest\n  conceded (19), best goal difference (+89) and biggest margin (+33).\n  PSG 2017/18 scored the most goals (108).\n- **Best season ever**: PSG 2015/16 — 2.55 ppg, the highest ever by a\n  Ligue 1 champion.\n- **Closest finishes**: Lens 1997/98 and Bordeaux 1998/99 both went to a\n  final round decider decided by goal difference at level points; Lille's\n  2020/21 title was won by one point over PSG.\n- **Biggest blowouts**: PSG 2015/16 (+33) is the largest margin ever; the\n  modern PSG machine repeated it in 2024/25 (+19 over Marseille).\n- **Records on the pitch**: PSG 9–0 Guingamp (2018/19) is the biggest win;\n  highest-scoring was Lyon 5–5 Marseille (2009/10).\n- **Top scorers** (StatsBomb coverage, 2015/16): Ibrahimović 36,\n  Lacazette 21, Cavani 19, Ben Arfa 17, Batshuayi 17.\n\n*Method notes: canonical names merged \"Olympique de Marseille\"/\"Marseille\"\netc.; 2026/27 excluded.*",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    }
  ]
}
